== Icons for rewards ==

Wouldn't it be nice to have 28px icons for each reward, as tested on my [[User:RayKoopa/Badges|user page]]? Properly done it requires templates for each accessory / eyes / mouth / clothing / hat (as done for the status effects, e.g. <nowiki>{{Scoutmaster Outfit}} in a Category:Clothing templates</nowiki>). - [[User:RayKoopa|RayKoopa]] ([[User talk:RayKoopa|talk]]) 18:44, 30 August 2025 (UTC)

:Yes this is being considered as a feature in the future. [[User:SavageAlien|SavageAlien]] ([[User talk:SavageAlien|talk]]) 23:04, 30 August 2025 (UTC)
::Want me to help with that? I could create the templates based on [[Template:Item]], using the prefixes of the image file names for the category (e.g. [[Template:Accessory]], [[Template:Eyes]], [[Template:Mouth]], [[Template:Outfit]], [[Template:Hat]]). Let me know if I should add you on Discord for discussion :) - [[User:RayKoopa|RayKoopa]] ([[User talk:RayKoopa|talk]]) 23:52, 30 August 2025 (UTC)
:Currently in the process of making a general-purpose [[Template:Cosmetic|template]] for cosmetics. [[User:Aw4yland|Aw4yland]] ([[User talk:Aw4yland|talk]]) 12:46, 6 September 2025 (UTC)
::Thanks, looking forward to use it :) I do wonder if, eventually, separate pages for each cosmetic would be useful. Right now, a lot of trivia is collected on the Passport] page, which could be moved to those pages then, having better context. - [[User:RayKoopa|RayKoopa]] ([[User talk:RayKoopa|talk]]) 13:50, 6 September 2025 (UTC)
::Done. Was Lua overkill? Yes, absolutely. Does it work? Also yes (<20 ms and 820 KB).
::"We do things not because they are easy, but because we thought they were easy".
::In hindsight, it would've been much faster to create a generic "icon+text" template (or adapt [[Template:Item]]) and just go with it. [[User:Aw4yland|Aw4yland]] ([[User talk:Aw4yland|talk]]) 15:48, 6 September 2025 (UTC)
:::Thanks! I previously noticed a handful of "specialties" in the file names of those accessoires that would've required a lot of template logic or even separate templates, but having a single template seems nicer! - [[User:RayKoopa|RayKoopa]] ([[User talk:RayKoopa|talk]]) 16:16, 6 September 2025 (UTC)

== Endurance badge ascent level ==

I added to the endurance badge section that it must be achieved above the tenderfoot difficulty. I based that on my own experience getting the badge and [https://www.reddit.com/r/PeakGame/comments/1merj23/struggling_with_the_endurance_badge_help this Reddit thread]. According to [[User:Aw4yland|<bdi>Aw4yland</bdi>]] this is not the case in the code. If anyone does not have this badge it would be appreciated if they could test this out. [[User:MaddyMurder|MaddyMurder]] ([[User talk:MaddyMurder|talk]]) 09:49, 18 September 2025 (UTC)

== Disaster Response Badge  ==

@[[User:Aw4yland|Aw4yland]] I am not overly familiar with the source code of the game but it seems that this segment of code from the RescueHook class is responsible for granting the Disaster Response Badge. Code extract is from v1.53.a.
<syntaxhighlight lang="csharp" line>
    private void FixedUpdate()
    {
        sinceFire += Time.fixedDeltaTime;
        if (isPulling)
        {
            if ((bool)targetPlayer)
            {
                targetPos = targetRig.position;
            }
            if (sinceFire > 0.25f)
            {
                if ((bool)targetPlayer)
                {
                    targetPlayer.refs.movement.ApplyExtraDrag(extraDragOther, ignoreRagdoll: true);
                    targetPlayer.data.sinceGrounded = Mathf.Clamp(targetPlayer.data.sinceGrounded, 0f, 1f);
                    if (photonView.IsMine)
                    {
                        Vector3 normalized = (base.transform.position - targetPlayer.Center).normalized;
                        Vector3 vector = Mathf.Clamp((base.transform.position - targetPlayer.Center).y, 0f, maxLiftDistance) * Vector3.up * liftDragForce;
                        Vector3 vector2 = dragForce * normalized;
                        vector2 *= pulLStrengthCurve.Evaluate(Vector3.Distance(base.transform.position, targetPlayer.Center));
                        targetPlayer.AddForceToBodyPart(targetRig, (vector2 + vector) * 0.2f, vector2 + vector);
                    }
                    if (!threwAchievement && photonView.IsMine)
                    {
                        float num = Vector3.Distance(rescuedCharacterStartingPos, targetPlayer.Center) * CharacterStats.unitsToMeters;
                        if (!targetPlayer.data.fullyConscious && num > 30f)
                        {
                            threwAchievement = true;
                            Singleton<AchievementManager>.Instance.ThrowAchievement(ACHIEVEMENTTYPE.DisasterResponseBadge);
                        }
                    }
</syntaxhighlight>
It seems that as long as the target player has been pulled over 30 m (distance between target's starting position and target's current position) and the target player is no longer fully conscious, the current player should unlock the badge if they haven't already. I think this should serve fine as a confirmation source. The relevant section of the article should prbably be reworded in a more objective manner. [[User:Pulse daemon|Pulse daemon]] ([[User talk:Pulse daemon|talk]]) 23:23, 1 February 2026 (UTC)

== Leave No Trace and the Scout Effigy ==

Anyone know whether using a Scout Effigy will spoil a Leave No Trace run? I only attempted that badge in singleplayer so I have no hard evidence of how they interact, but since you have to place the effigy like the other disallowed items in order to activate it, my guess is that it does. [[User:CameoAppearance|CameoAppearance]] ([[User talk:CameoAppearance|talk]]) 14:06, 21 February 2026 (UTC)

== RV of row header usage ==

@[[User:SavageAlien|SavageAlien]]: Why did you revert my addition of row headers to the table? It makes the table easier to understand for screen readers & other accessibility tools, since it explicitly associates everything else in the row with the badge's name. {&#123;'''[[User:Lemondoge1|Lemondoge1]]'''&#124;[[User talk:Lemondoge1|Talk]]&#124;[[Special:Contributions/Lemondoge1|Contributions]]&#125;} 22:43, 9 September 2026 (UTC)

:It ruined the visual appearance of the table in the process.
:May I ask if you have a screen reader or similar tool that you use?
:Some changes to the visual design are required to properly support what you were aiming to accomplish while preserving visual design.
:If you have a tool that you use, that would be useful for testing and troubleshooting future accessibility support. [[User:SavageAlien|SavageAlien]] ([[User talk:SavageAlien|talk]]) 22:50, 9 September 2026 (UTC)
::I occasionally demo accessibility with Windows Narrator, although I do not use it regularly. Admittedly, I don't notice a difference in Windows Narrator demoing it now, but in accessibility tutorial videos, I've seen screen readers use row headers in place of announcing "row 1" / "row 2" / "row 3" / etc.
::I do notice now that I forgot to pipe some of the <code>scope="col"</code> bits of the table, which goofed it a bit, but otherwise I did not see any unexpected changes in the table's appearance (just that the name cell text was centered and the cells given a different background color, as expected). Was it glitched on mobile or on other skins? {&#123;'''[[User:Lemondoge1|Lemondoge1]]'''&#124;[[User talk:Lemondoge1|Talk]]&#124;[[Special:Contributions/Lemondoge1|Contributions]]&#125;} 23:41, 9 September 2026 (UTC)
